@* {{details: Full restart procedure}} … {{end}}: the browser's own fold. A native details
   element rather than a script-driven one, so it opens with the keyboard, is announced as
   a disclosure by screen readers, and works before the circuit has started.

   What is inside was cut out of the source and rendered as a piece of its own (see
   Runbook), so it may hold anything a page can: cards, buttons, {{if}} sections. Those keep
   updating while the fold is closed — they are in the page, only not shown — which is what
   lets a fold be opened on an answer that is already current.

   The open attribute is written only from the shortcode. A render that does not change it
   leaves the element alone, so a fold somebody opened stays open through every sweep. *@

<details class="md-details" open="@Open">
    <summary class="md-details-summary">@Title</summary>
    <div class="md-details-body">@ChildContent</div>
</details>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the fold says while it is closed. Drawn as text.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>Whether it starts open, from <c>open=true</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Open { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
